# Internal development documentation: ignore file.
#
# The repository is public. This directory holds the project's working
# documentation: planning, process and local state. None of it is published and
# none of it is referenced by the product, so none of it may be committed.
#
# The published documentation lives directly in this directory (commenting.md)
# and the consumer-facing documentation lives on the website.
#
# The rule below ignores everything in this directory and then re-admits the
# files that are meant to be public. A document that is meant to be published
# must be re-admitted here in the same way.

*
!.gitignore

# The published documentation of this repository. Everything else in this
# directory is internal, and a document that is meant to be published has to be
# re-admitted here explicitly.
!commenting.md
!installation.md
!configuration.md
!components.md
!accessibility.md
!cli.md
!migration.md
